DECL	{"assumptions":[],"binders":["subject"],"id":"NRS_484D_400_5","intentions":[],"laws":["NRS-484D-400-5"],"narrowings":[],"operationalizations":[],"residues":["A permission about equipment and its audible range; it imposes no duty on conduct and the rule judges only whether the siren sounds.","Restates the permission the exception (s4, s5) grants: in that event the siren may sound. The purpose 'to warn pedestrians and other drivers of his or her approach' is what a sounding siren does; the duty is the same whether or not these words are read.","A permission to show warning lamps without the siren; it imposes no duty, and the siren duty never judges lamps alone."],"surrogate":false}
